Padic -- p-adic numbers
***********************

Description
===========

The field of $p$-adic numbers $\QQ_p$ consists of all formal Laurent series
$$\sum_{n=\nu}^\infty a_n p^n = a_\nu p^\nu + a_{\nu+1} p^{\nu+1} + \cdots,$$
where $\nu \in \ZZ$ and $a_n \in \{0, \ldots, p - 1\}$, together with the usual
operations of addition and multiplication in base $p$, with carrying that may
continue indefinitely.  Equivalently, $\QQ_p$ is the completion of $\QQ$ with
respect to the $p$-adic absolute value $|x|_p = p^{-\nu_p(x)}$, just as $\RR$
is the completion of $\QQ$ under the usual absolute value.

Elements of $\QQ_p$ are created by applying a *note p-adic field family:
PadicFieldFamily, to a rational number.  They are stored and displayed as
truncated series, with a default *note precision: precision_lpPadicNumber_rp,
of 20 base-$p$ digits.

+--------------------------+
|i1 : x = QQ_7(12/7)       |
|                          |
|o1 = 5*7^-1 + 1           |
|                          |
|o1 : QQ  (of precision 20)|
|       7                  |
+--------------------------+

This package is implemented using the *note ForeignFunctions:
(ForeignFunctions)Top, package to call $p$-adic arithmetic routines from the
FLINT (see https://flintlib.org/ ) C library.

See the paper Implementing p-adic numbers in Macaulay2 using its foreign
function interface and FLINT (see https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.16799 ) for more
information.

* Menu:

* PadicFieldFamily::            class for p-adic fields
* PadicNumber::                 base class for p-adic numbers

