unit -- unit part of a p-adic number
************************************

  * Usage: 
        unit x
  * Inputs:
      * x, a *note p-adic number: PadicNumber,, 
  * Outputs:
      * an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 

Description
===========

Every $x\in\QQ_p$ can be decomposed into a product $x=up^\nu$, where
$u\in\ZZ_p^\times$, i.e., it is a unit in the ring of $p$-adic integers. This
function returns $u$ as an integer.

+--------------------------+
|i1 : x = QQ_7 (1/49)      |
|                          |
|o1 = 1*7^-2               |
|                          |
|o1 : QQ  (of precision 20)|
|       7                  |
+--------------------------+
|i2 : unit x               |
|                          |
|o2 = 1                    |
+--------------------------+

Note that in general, $u$ has infinitely many $p$-adic digits.  Therefore, it
is truncated based on the *note precision: precision_lpPadicNumber_rp, of $x$.

+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : x = QQ_7(-1/49)                                                      |
|                                                                          |
|o3 = 6*7^-2 + 6*7^-1 + 6 + 6*7^1 + 6*7^2 + 6*7^3 + 6*7^4 + 6*7^5 + 6*7^6 +|
|     6*7^7 + 6*7^8 + 6*7^9 + 6*7^10 + 6*7^11 + 6*7^12 + 6*7^13 + 6*7^14 + |
|     6*7^15 + 6*7^16 + 6*7^17 + 6*7^18 + 6*7^19                           |
|                                                                          |
|o3 : QQ  (of precision 20)                                                |
|       7                                                                  |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : unit x                                                               |
|                                                                          |
|o4 = 3909821048582988048                                                  |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+

