pVal -- p-adic valuation of a p-adic number
*******************************************

  * Usage: 
        pVal x
  * Inputs:
      * x, a *note p-adic number: PadicNumber,, 
  * Outputs:
      * an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, or *note InfiniteNumber:
        (Macaulay2Doc)InfiniteNumber, if x is zero

Description
===========

Returns the $p$-adic valuation $\nu_p(x)$, i.e., the exponent $\nu$ in the
factorization $x = u p^\nu$ where $u$ is a $p$-adic unit.

+-------------------+
|i1 : pVal QQ_7 49  |
|                   |
|o1 = 2             |
+-------------------+
|i2 : pVal QQ_7(1/7)|
|                   |
|o2 = -1            |
+-------------------+
|i3 : pVal QQ_7 0   |
|                   |
|o3 = infinity      |
|                   |
|o3 : InfiniteNumber|
+-------------------+

See also
========

  * *note unit: unit, -- unit part of a p-adic number
  * *note abs(PadicNumber): abs_lpPadicNumber_rp, -- p-adic absolute value

Ways to use pVal:
=================

