PadicNumber == PadicNumber -- equality of p-adic numbers
********************************************************

  * Operator: *note ==: (Macaulay2Doc)==,
  * Usage: 
        x == y
  * Inputs:
      * x, a *note p-adic number: PadicNumber,, 
      * y, a *note p-adic number: PadicNumber,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, 

Description
===========

Test equality of two $p$-adic numbers.  Numbers in the same field are compared
directly.

+---------------------+
|i1 : QQ_7 3 == QQ_7 3|
|                     |
|o1 = true            |
+---------------------+
|i2 : QQ_7 3 == QQ_7 4|
|                     |
|o2 = false           |
+---------------------+

If the two numbers lie in different $p$-adic fields, or if one argument is an
ordinary number, equality is tested by comparing their lifts to *note QQ:
(Macaulay2Doc)QQ,.

+---------------------+
|i3 : QQ_7 3 == QQ_5 3|
|                     |
|o3 = true            |
+---------------------+
|i4 : QQ_7 3 == 3     |
|                     |
|o4 = true            |
+---------------------+
|i5 : 3 == QQ_7 3     |
|                     |
|o5 = true            |
+---------------------+

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * "Number == PadicNumber"
  * "PadicNumber == Number"
  * *note PadicNumber == PadicNumber: PadicNumber == PadicNumber, -- equality
    of p-adic numbers
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

