PadicNumber << ZZ -- multiply a p-adic number by a power of p
*************************************************************

  * Operator: *note <<: (Macaulay2Doc)<<,
  * Usage: 
        x << n
  * Inputs:
      * x, a *note p-adic number: PadicNumber,, 
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note p-adic number: PadicNumber,, x times p^n; 

Description
===========

Returns $x \cdot p^n$, shifting the $p$-adic expansion left by $n$ places. A
negative shift divides by $p^{|n|}$.

+--------------------------+
|i1 : QQ_7 3 << 2          |
|                          |
|o1 = 3*7^2                |
|                          |
|o1 : QQ  (of precision 20)|
|       7                  |
+--------------------------+
|i2 : QQ_7 3 << -1         |
|                          |
|o2 = 3*7^-1               |
|                          |
|o2 : QQ  (of precision 20)|
|       7                  |
+--------------------------+
* Menu:

* PadicNumber >> ZZ::           divide a p-adic number by a power of p

Ways to use this method:
========================

