teichmullerLift -- Teichmüller lift of a p-adic integer
*******************************************************

  * Usage: 
        teichmullerLift x
  * Inputs:
      * x, a *note p-adic number: PadicNumber,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note p-adic number: PadicNumber,, 

Description
===========

Returns the Teichmüller lift of $x$, which is the unique root of unity $t \in
\ZZ_p^\times$ satisfying $t \equiv x \pmod{p}$ and $t^p = t$.

+----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : t = teichmullerLift QQ_7 3                                             |
|                                                                            |
|o1 = 3 + 4*7^1 + 6*7^2 + 3*7^3 + 2*7^5 + 6*7^6 + 2*7^7 + 4*7^8 + 3*7^9 +    |
|     4*7^10 + 4*7^11 + 5*7^12 + 2*7^13 + 1*7^14 + 2*7^15 + 1*7^16 + 4*7^17 +|
|     6*7^18 + 1*7^19                                                        |
|                                                                            |
|o1 : QQ  (of precision 20)                                                  |
|       7                                                                    |
+----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : t^7 == t                                                               |
|                                                                            |
|o2 = true                                                                   |
+----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

An error is raised if $\nu_p(x) < 0$, i.e., if $x$ is not a $p$-adic integer.

Ways to use teichmullerLift:
============================

  * "teichmullerLift(PadicNumber)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note teichmullerLift: teichmullerLift, is a *note method function:
(Macaulay2Doc)MethodFunction,.

