lift(PadicNumber,type of ZZ) -- lift a p-adic number to another ring
********************************************************************

  * Function: *note lift: (Macaulay2Doc)lift,
  * Usage: 
        lift(x, R)
        x^R
  * Inputs:
      * x, a *note p-adic number: PadicNumber,, 
      * R, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, a *note rational number:
        (Macaulay2Doc)QQ,, or a *note p-adic number: PadicNumber,,
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Verify => ..., default value true
  * Outputs:
      * a *note number: (Macaulay2Doc)Number,, an element of R; 

Description
===========

Lift a $p$-adic number to an other ring.  This is only well-defined when R to
*note ZZ: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, *note QQ: (Macaulay2Doc)QQ,, or the $p$-adic field
containing x.

+--------------------------+
|i1 : x = QQ_7 49          |
|                          |
|o1 = 1*7^2                |
|                          |
|o1 : QQ  (of precision 20)|
|       7                  |
+--------------------------+
|i2 : lift(x, ZZ)          |
|                          |
|o2 = 49                   |
+--------------------------+
|i3 : lift(x, QQ)          |
|                          |
|o3 = 49                   |
|                          |
|o3 : QQ                   |
+--------------------------+
|i4 : lift(x, QQ_7)        |
|                          |
|o4 = 1*7^2                |
|                          |
|o4 : QQ  (of precision 20)|
|       7                  |
+--------------------------+

As usual, the *note ^: (Macaulay2Doc)^, operator is a shorthand for this
operation.

+--------------------------+
|i5 : x^ZZ                 |
|                          |
|o5 = 49                   |
+--------------------------+
|i6 : x^QQ                 |
|                          |
|o6 = 49                   |
|                          |
|o6 : QQ                   |
+--------------------------+
|i7 : x^(QQ_7)             |
|                          |
|o7 = 1*7^2                |
|                          |
|o7 : QQ  (of precision 20)|
|       7                  |
+--------------------------+

Caveat
======

Lifting to *note ZZ: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ, raises an error if the $p$-adic
valuation of x is negative.

See also
========

  * *note promote(ZZ,type of PadicNumber): promote_lpZZ_cmtype of
    PadicNumber_rp, -- promote a number to a p-adic field

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * "lift(PadicNumber,type of PadicNumber)"
  * "lift(PadicNumber,type of QQ)"
  * *note lift(PadicNumber,type of ZZ): lift_lpPadicNumber_cmtype of ZZ_rp, --
    lift a p-adic number to another ring
