interval(PadicNumber,PadicNumber) -- convert p-adic numbers to a real interval
******************************************************************************

  * Function: *note interval: (Macaulay2Doc)interval,
  * Usage: 
        interval(x, y)
        interval x
  * Inputs:
      * x, a *note p-adic number: PadicNumber, or a *note number:
        (Macaulay2Doc)Number,,
      * y, a *note p-adic number: PadicNumber, or a *note number:
        (Macaulay2Doc)Number,,
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Precision => ..., default value -1
  * Outputs:
      * a *note real interval: (Macaulay2Doc)RRi,, 

Description
===========

Converts a $p$-adic number to a real interval by first lifting to *note QQ:
(Macaulay2Doc)QQ,. When two arguments are given, returns the interval with
those endpoints.

+-----------------------------+
|i1 : interval QQ_7 5         |
|                             |
|o1 = [5,5]                   |
|                             |
|o1 : RRi (of precision 53)   |
+-----------------------------+
|i2 : interval(QQ_7 5, QQ_7 6)|
|                             |
|o2 = [5,6]                   |
|                             |
|o2 : RRi (of precision 53)   |
+-----------------------------+
|i3 : interval(QQ_7 5, 6)     |
|                             |
|o3 = [5,6]                   |
|                             |
|o3 : RRi (of precision 53)   |
+-----------------------------+
|i4 : interval(5, QQ_7 6)     |
|                             |
|o4 = [5,6]                   |
|                             |
|o4 : RRi (of precision 53)   |
+-----------------------------+

See also
========

